{
  "_comment": "THE FISHING CONTENT. One file, read by both halves: server/build.rs compiles it into the module (server/src/genre/fishing/), game/fishing/fishing_data.gd loads it on the client. What a catch IS (category, weight, value), where it lives (spot loot tables), what gear does, and every timing the cast and the bite run on. Mechanics and most of the catalog are carried over from Fishing for Compliments ('Bottom Feeders'); junk and treasure are the Fantasy Props kit's models, which is what the catch fly-out shows.",
  "levels": ["lakeside", "meadow"],
  "version": 1,

  "timing": {
    "_comment": "Seconds. The bite is rolled from the cast's seed between bite_min_s and bite_max_s, then divided by the spot's bite_speed and its richness factor, and never longer than bite_cap_s: the slowest spot, fished out and crowded, came to a minute's wait, which is a player walking away. The bobber twitches for tell_lead_s before it goes under; from the moment it does, a press inside hookset_window_s (x the reel's hookset_window_mult) sets the hook. Inside hookset_perfect_s it is PERFECT, after hookset_late_s it is LATE. A press faster than min_reaction_s is a guess, not a reaction, and is refused. clock_slack_s is how early the server will believe a bite happened, for clock skew between it and the client.",
    "bite_min_s": 2.0,
    "bite_max_s": 7.0,
    "bite_cap_s": 30.0,
    "tell_lead_s": 0.9,
    "hookset_window_s": 0.85,
    "hookset_perfect_s": 0.30,
    "hookset_late_s": 0.62,
    "min_reaction_s": 0.08,
    "clock_slack_s": 0.35,
    "line_life_s": 150.0
  },

  "cast": {
    "_comment": "Metres. A cast must land at least min_range_m out (a float dropped at your feet is not a cast) and no further than the rod's max_cast_m plus range_slack_m, which covers the rod tip being ahead of the body and a position a frame old.",
    "min_range_m": 4.0,
    "range_slack_m": 2.0
  },

  "economy": {
    "_comment": "SPOTS DEPLETE, and it is the server's number, not each client's. Every catch landed in a spot takes depletion_per_catch off its richness; it grows back at regen_per_second, never below richness_floor. A fished-out spot bites slower, so the lake keeps moving. Each OTHER line already in the same spot slows your bite by crowding_penalty.",
    "depletion_per_catch": 0.08,
    "regen_per_second": 0.004,
    "richness_floor": 0.25,
    "crowding_penalty": 0.15
  },

